  "interpretation": "<ol><li><p>Positive Result:</p><ul><li>A positive GeneXpert test result indicates the presence of the target genetic sequence(s) associated with the specific infectious agent or disease. For example, in the case of TB, a positive result would suggest the presence of Mycobacterium tuberculosis, the bacterium responsible for TB infection. Positive results may also include information about drug resistance, if applicable.</li></ul></li><li><p>Negative Result:</p><ul><li>A negative GeneXpert test result indicates that the target genetic sequence(s) associated with the specific infectious agent or disease were not detected in the sample. However, a negative result does not completely rule out the possibility of infection or disease, especially in cases with a low number of microorganisms or if the sample was not collected correctly.</li></ul></li><li><p>Indeterminate Result:</p><ul><li>In some instances, the GeneXpert test may yield an indeterminate result, which means that the test did not provide a clear positive or negative result. This may occur due to technical issues with the test or an insufficient amount of genetic material in the sample.</li></ul></li></ol>",
